.TH OPACITY 1 opacity-VERSION
.SH NAME
opacity \- get or set a window's opacity (_NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opacity
.I window-id
[
.I 0..1
]
[
.B \-v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opacity
gets or sets the EWMH
.BR _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY
property of the specified window. Without a value argument, the current
opacity is printed as a floating point number in the range 0.0..1.0 along with
its raw 32-bit hexadecimal representation. When a value is supplied, it must be
in the range 0.0..1.0 and the corresponding 32-bit cardinal is written to the
window property.
.PP
If the property is not present, many compositors treat the window as fully
opaque; in that case
.B opacity
prints
.I 1.000000 (unset)
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non-zero on error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Read opacity of window 0x3e00007:
.B opacity 0x3e00007
.TP
Set opacity to 75%:
.B opacity 0x3e00007 0.75
